export anchor SurfReportStyle:
    number: 138
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Surf report
    idea: A beach shack surf forecast where the week is a smooth swell chart, projects are breaks in a forecast table, and progress stands up as rounded waves.
    base: light
    palette:
        sand: #f7eedb, the page and sheet rows
        foam: #fffaf0, panels and text on deep sea
        sea: #0e6973, nav, table head and the swell line
        deep: #0b3d4a, header, headings and big numbers
        shallow: #cdeef0, swell fill, condition tiles and focus fill
        sun: #f7c948, primary button and sun disc, never text
        coral: #b23a2f, the Behind flag and the overdue banner
        coralSoft: #f6c6b8, the overdue tile and avatar
        driftwood: #4a3a2a, body text
        bark: #6a5644, captions and row keys
        palm: #1f6f3c, the On track sun
        rust: #8a5300, the At risk fin
    type:
        Rounded sans for headings and numbers uses Arial Rounded MT Bold,
        Varela Round, Nunito, Trebuchet MS, Verdana. Body uses Verdana,
        Tahoma, DejaVu Sans. Tile numbers 38px, greeting 36px, section
        titles 22px, chart labels 13px bold, body 14px at 1.55, captions
        11px caps tracked 0.1em.
    layout:
        A deep sea header holds a sun over wave logo, a pill search, a
        yellow pill New project with a ledge, a round bell and the user,
        over a sea nav with rounded top tabs where the current tab is sand.
        The first row pairs a Today's report panel with a corner sun, the
        greeting, a coral overdue banner and four rounded condition tiles,
        with a wide swell chart panel showing a smooth filled curve with
        dots and values for the 14 days and two total pills. The Break
        forecast is a table with projects as columns and rows for
        conditions, progress as rounded wave bars, tasks done and due, which
        scrolls sideways inside its panel on small screens. Below are a
        Beach log and a key panel explaining the three status icons.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 20 to 24px padding in panels, 24 to 28px between sections.
    density: Relaxed. Big rounded numbers, one forecast table, generous line height.
    corners: Very soft. 24px panels, 16 to 18px tiles, 22px pill buttons, wave bars rounded on top.
    borders: Mostly none. Dotted 2px sand lines between table cells and log rows.
    shadows: Only the primary button, a 3px solid darker sun ledge below it.
    icons: Chunky filled beach signs at 30px above the word. Rayed sun On track, fin over a wave At risk, square beach flag Behind, rounded exclamation tile for overdue.
    focus: A 3px dashed deep sea outline offset 3px with a shallow fill, sun yellow on dark bars.
    tone: Laid back, such as Today's report, Heads up, Break forecast, Beach log and how the week is breaking.
